1
00:00:04,727 --> 00:00:09,354
Whiskers and Luna's World. Episode eight. The Frozen Poles!

2
00:00:16,349 --> 00:00:20,174
One chilly morning, Luna was spinning her old globe.

3
00:00:20,374 --> 00:00:24,834
Luna, your globe has whipped cream on top. And on the bottom! Yum!

4
00:00:25,034 --> 00:00:29,737
That's not cream, Whiskers. It's ice! The very top of the Earth is the North Pole.

5
00:00:29,937 --> 00:00:31,939
And the very bottom is the South Pole.

6
00:00:32,139 --> 00:00:36,620
A pole? A giant stripy pole sticking out? Perfect for scratching!

7
00:00:40,660 --> 00:00:42,882
Let's go and see if there's really a pole!

8
00:00:53,421 --> 00:00:55,764
Whoosh! Up into space they flew.

9
00:00:55,964 --> 00:01:00,824
Look! The North Pole is the very top of the Earth. The South Pole is the very bottom.

10
00:01:05,160 --> 00:01:07,131
I don't see any pole sticking out.

11
00:01:14,126 --> 00:01:18,334
On a map, the North Pole is at the top, and the South Pole is at the bottom.

12
00:01:18,534 --> 00:01:20,547
Let's go to the bottom first. South!

13
00:01:34,337 --> 00:01:38,352
They landed in Antarctica, at the bottom of the world.

14
00:01:42,983 --> 00:01:45,730
Hello! Welcome to Antarctica! I'm Pebble.

15
00:01:45,930 --> 00:01:48,459
Hi, Pebble! Is this ice floating on the sea?

16
00:01:48,659 --> 00:01:52,807
No! Under the ice there is land. A whole continent, covered in thick ice!

17
00:01:59,506 --> 00:02:04,020
Lots of penguins live down here, in the south. But I've never met a polar bear!

18
00:02:04,220 --> 00:02:07,676
Please give one a message: Hello from the bottom of the world!

19
00:02:07,876 --> 00:02:10,732
Why send a message? Come with us! Hop on!

20
00:02:21,272 --> 00:02:24,446
So they flew north, with a penguin on board.

21
00:02:29,373 --> 00:02:32,711
Phew! It's getting so hot! I'm a penguin, not a fried egg!

22
00:02:32,911 --> 00:02:37,272
Whiskers, stop! Penguins live in the south. Polar bears live in the north.

23
00:02:37,472 --> 00:02:38,656
So they never meet!

24
00:02:44,173 --> 00:02:49,367
I knew that. I gave Pebble a sauna on purpose. Penguins love saunas.

25
00:02:49,567 --> 00:02:50,764
We do not!

26
00:02:53,918 --> 00:02:57,576
So they took Pebble home, and carried the message north.

27
00:03:11,366 --> 00:03:14,362
Then, at the top of the world: the Arctic!

28
00:03:14,562 --> 00:03:17,388
Look! An Arctic fox! And walruses, and seals!

29
00:03:17,588 --> 00:03:20,256
But where's the pole? Not even a little one!

30
00:03:23,410 --> 00:03:29,245
Ho ho! I'm Bjorn. There's no real pole, little cat. The North Pole is just the very top of the Earth.

31
00:03:29,445 --> 00:03:33,249
From Pebble the penguin: Hello from the bottom of the world!

32
00:03:33,449 --> 00:03:37,246
A penguin! I've never met one. Tell Pebble: Hello from the top!

33
00:03:40,105 --> 00:03:46,039
And here, there's no land under the ice! Just the Arctic Ocean. The ice floats, like an ice cube in a drink.

34
00:03:52,147 --> 00:03:54,499
Brr! But why are the poles so cold?

35
00:03:54,699 --> 00:03:58,949
In the middle of the Earth, the sunshine comes straight down. Strong and hot!

36
00:03:59,149 --> 00:04:03,036
But here, it comes in at a slant. It spreads out thin, so it's weak.

37
00:04:10,917 --> 00:04:15,567
In summer, the sun doesn't set for weeks. In winter, it stays dark for weeks!

38
00:04:21,675 --> 00:04:24,716
Weeks and weeks of night? The best nap ever!

39
00:04:24,916 --> 00:04:26,419
And look! The northern lights!

40
00:04:35,482 --> 00:04:40,934
Remember! One. The North Pole is at the top of the Earth, the South Pole at the bottom.

41
00:04:43,201 --> 00:04:47,408
Two. Polar bears live in the north. Penguins live in the south.

42
00:04:49,676 --> 00:04:54,946
Three. The poles are the coldest places, because the sun's light there is weak.

43
00:05:01,054 --> 00:05:06,443
Quiz time! Which pole is at the top of the Earth? The North Pole, or the South Pole?

44
00:05:09,893 --> 00:05:11,915
The North Pole! Well done!

45
00:05:14,183 --> 00:05:18,783
Next. Where do penguins live? Near the North Pole, or the South Pole?

46
00:05:22,233 --> 00:05:24,847
Near the South Pole! Great job!

47
00:05:32,137 --> 00:05:35,304
Pebble and Bjorn will never meet. But now they're pen pals!

48
00:05:35,504 --> 00:05:39,496
Being the mail cat is hard work. Time for a polar nap.

49
00:05:43,536 --> 00:05:46,528
Next time: weather and seasons! Goodnight!

